From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:25:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmgr-pwrstate: hold a domain off at
 probe for a wakeup path

A domain found off when the PMGR driver probes gets no
GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP, so genpd powers it off in the noirq phase of
a system sleep even under a device on the wakeup path. On T8132 the
SIO's domain, sio_cpu, is such a domain: with the SIO's stop handed to
the sleep's commit and the SIO on the wakeup path, sio_cpu still went
off before syscore (flags 0x2, power word target 0), and the commit
then read a powered-down SIO.

Give every domain the driver controls ACTIVE_WAKEUP, as the domains on
at probe already have; keep DEFER_OFF for those alone. With it, sio_cpu
stays on through syscore (measured under pm_test=core with the flag set
at run time).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
index 12fa9d0033..dfb9caf98e 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
@@ -1012,8 +1012,15 @@ static int apple_pmgr_ps_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			active = apple_pmgr_ps_set(&ps->genpd, APPLE_PMGR_PS_ACTIVE,
 						   !ps->no_auto_enable && !ps->no_auto_pm) == 0;
 		}
-	} else if (active && !ps->firmware_owned && !ps->inherited_on) {
-		ps->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_DEFER_OFF | GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP;
+	} else if (!ps->firmware_owned && !ps->inherited_on) {
+		/*
+		 * A device on the wakeup path holds its domain through system sleep,
+		 * whether or not the domain was on when it was found: a coprocessor
+		 * powered up later (SIO) still needs it until its stop at the commit.
+		 */
+		ps->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP;
+		if (active)
+			ps->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_DEFER_OFF;
 	}
 
 	/* Turn on auto-PM if the domain is already on, unless it must stay off */
-- 
